{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableauBot","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableauBot","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux_bot","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableauBot.lean#L28-L48","doc":"**`#SYT(⊥) = 1`.** The empty Young diagram has exactly one standard Young\ntableau. Proved directly by `Subsingleton` (every entry is `0` by `zeros`, as `⊥`\nhas no cells) + `Nonempty` (the all-zero `highestWeight ⊥`, whose `BijOn` onto\n`Set.Icc 1 (⊥.cells.card) = Set.Icc 1 0 = ∅` is `Set.bijOn_empty`), then\n`Nat.card_eq_one_iff_unique`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}